    </region>
    <region left="18" top="540" width="529" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12" isBreakable="false">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 12px;">2  a range variable, then plain assignments      no for loop anywhere</p>
      </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="576" width="1327" height="21" color="#000000" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">The sweep is spaced logarithmically, 1201 points over the two decades 0.1 to 10 - 600 per decade. Even spacing put only a fifth of the points below resonance, which is where every peak is, so the curves came out of the pane as straight segments.</p>
      </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="603" width="133" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
