    <region left="18" top="6255" width="194" height="26" color="#000000" fontSize="12" isBreakable="false">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 12px;">what the answer means</p>
      </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="6291" width="1321" height="49" color="#000000" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">T1 shows eight lines  -&gt;  a pane builds its curves from the input, and the design guide gain figure becomes ONE frame with six loads and both marker lines. T1 shows four  -&gt;  the pane is the ceiling; with a linear y that is four traces a frame and the</p>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">figure stays split. T1 empty or red  -&gt;  the count must match, and T3 then says whether under-feeding is allowed either.</p>
      </content>
      </text>
    </region>
  </regions>
</worksheet>